    "narratives": {
      "Description": "When package.json pin and installed node_modules disagree, hooks fail closed and print AC9.7 global install plus repair. Settled OVPR (#5798, AC9.12) says project package-manager install is the fix for that skew; repair is for deposits after the pin is installed.",
      "ImplementationPlan": "1. Update install-health cheap/constants guidance and hook-dispatch printing so pin≠installed names project npm/pnpm install when only node_modules lags, and names repair only when deposits lag a good pin.\n2. Add focused tests proving the guidance cases and that ordinary shells stay fail-closed; do not revive #5956 allow-list mega-design.",
      "UserStory": "As an agent or human after a pin bump, I want the mismatch refusal to tell me to run a project package-manager install, so that I can sync node_modules without a useless global reinstall.",
      "Traces": "#6013"
    },
    "items": [
